<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carloman of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 830–880</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carloman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> was a Carolingian king of Bavaria from 876 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from 877, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a>. After Emperor Louis II died in 875 without a son, Carloman contested Italy with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> and took the Italian crown after Charles's death. Illness forced him to give up power, and he died in 880, leaving Bavaria to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-younger">Louis the Younger</a> and Italy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat">Charles the Fat</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carloman-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Carloman of Bavaria" width="220" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ekkehard von Aura · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carloman_of_Bavaria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
